  e_flat  mean residual (P - modelled sigma^2) on FLAT patches, DN^2
  e_ped   the 5th frame-percentile of the residual on TEXTURED patches, DN^2
  cv_tail coefficient of variation of S over the least-sharp half of the
          frames: near 0 means the residual really is frame-invariant.

  log e_flat vs log level: slope +1.83 (R2 0.97) over 6 stacks.
  slope ~2 would indicate PRNU (fixed-pattern, variance ~ (frac.S)^2);
  slope ~1 would indicate a gain error in the photon-transfer model;
  slope ~0 would indicate a read-noise offset.

